# Restart local services when needed

The project runs locally (not only Docker):

- API: `go run ./cmd/api` in `backend`, port `18080`, env from `.env`
- Frontend: Vite `npm run dev` in `frontend`, port `15173` (hot reload — do not restart unless it is down)
- Postgres: `postgres://postgres:123@localhost:5432/sbis`

When you change Go code, SQL migrations, `.env`, or the API would otherwise keep serving old binaries:

1. Apply pending migrations to the local database (`migrate up` or equivalent SQL).
2. Stop the process listening on `18080` (and its parent `go run` if present).
3. Start the API again with `.env` loaded into the process environment.
4. Wait until `GET http://localhost:18080/health` returns 200.

Do this yourself. Do not tell the user to restart the API.
